{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "locale": "zh",
  "kind": "employment_concept_lexicon",
  "purpose": "Chinese surface phrases for the deterministic employment-code analyzer. Chinese-speaking residents describe their work in Chinese; without this pool the analyzer returned nothing at all for inputs like 我在酒店打扫客房.",
  "important": [
    "This file contains NO official classification codes. It only maps Chinese",
    "surface phrases onto the SAME occupation_terms / industry_terms already used",
    "by the Korean lexicon, so retrieval reaches the identical official KSCO8 /",
    "KSIC11 rows. A term with no match in the official table produces no candidate.",
    "",
    "occupation_terms describe what the PERSON does; industry_terms describe what",
    "the EMPLOYER's business is. The two tracks are never mixed.",
    "",
    "Han surfaces are matched by substring from length 2 (see surfaceHits in",
    "scripts/employment_code_analyzer.mjs) because Chinese is written without",
    "spaces and a 2-character word is already specific."
  ],
